Starts a writer on NIM for one document of your topic's corpus, under the file name you give in your topic's directory. The writer sees none of your chat: the brief says what the document covers and for whom, which maps and items it draws on, the pages to cite, and what it leaves to the other documents. It writes with write_document and reports, which wakes you. To change a document, start a writer for the same file with a brief saying what to change. tips-and-tricks.md is a document like any other, and every topic has one.
